  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Welcome, World Explorer!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "This is a **check-in**, not a test. It helps us find out what you already know about our world so your lessons can be a perfect fit. Have a go at everything!"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "emoji": "🗺️",
      "alt": "Explore the world",
      "caption": "Explore the world"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 1: Maps and the world"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Earth has **7 continents**: Asia, Africa, North America, South America, Antarctica, Europe and Australia/Oceania. There are **5 oceans**: Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Southern and Arctic. **Asia** is the biggest continent and the **Pacific** is the biggest ocean."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "Which is the largest continent?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Africa"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Asia"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Europe"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "b"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 2: Inventions and history"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "People have invented things that changed the world: the **wheel**, the **printing press**, the **light bulb**, the **telephone** and the **computer**. History is the story of what happened long ago, and we learn about it from objects, buildings and writing."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "Which invention helps us make light at night?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Light bulb"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Wheel"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Printing press"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "a"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "activity",
      "title": "Inventor's challenge",
      "materials": [
        "paper",
        "pencil"
      ],
      "instructions": [
        "Think of a problem at home, like a heavy school bag.",
        "Draw an invention that solves it.",
        "Label the parts and explain how it works."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 3: Space and nature"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Our Solar System has **8 planets** that go round the Sun. Earth is the third planet from the Sun. The **Moon** goes around the Earth. The **Amazon** is the biggest rainforest and the **Sahara** is a huge desert."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "How many planets are in our Solar System?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "7"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "8"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "9"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "b"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 4: Healthy living and helpful habits"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "A healthy body needs a **balanced diet**: fruit, vegetables, protein, grains and water. We need exercise and **8 to 10 hours of sleep** at your age. Good habits include washing hands and brushing teeth."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "true_false",
        "prompt": "A balanced diet means eating only one kind of food.",
        "answer": [
          false
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 5: Languages, flags and fun facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "People around the world speak thousands of languages. Every country has a **flag** and a **capital city**. For example, Paris is the capital of France and Tokyo is the capital of Japan."
    },
    {
      "type": "reveal",
      "prompt": "What is a fact you know about another country?",
      "answer_markdown": "Any fact is good! Ask a grown-up and look it up on a map together."
    },
    {
      "type": "summary",
      "points": [
        "There are 7 continents and 5 oceans.",
        "Inventions change how we live.",
        "Our Solar System has 8 planets.",
        "A balanced diet, exercise and sleep keep us healthy.",
        "Countries have flags and capital cities."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "style": "tip",
      "markdown": "Ready? Start the quiz. 12 questions, about 15 minutes. Good luck!"
    }
  ],
